<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%- include('partials/head', {
      metaDescription: 'PictoCard for Wii is a free Homebrew Channel app for sending PictoCards from your Wii: pick a photo from your SD card, add a Mii, and send it by email or to a Wii Message Board.',
      ogTitle: 'PictoCard for Wii - Send Cards from Your Wii',
      ogDescription: 'A free Homebrew Channel app for sending PictoCards from your Wii',
      ogUrl: domain + '/wii-app',
      canonicalUrl: domain + '/wii-app'
    }) %>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%- include('partials/header') %>

    <main class="container wii-app">
      <section class="hero">
        <h1>PictoCard for Wii</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Send PictoCards right from your Wii. Pick a photo from your SD card, add a Mii from your
          Wii, and send it by email or to a Wii Message Board with WiiLink.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="wii-app-layout">
        <section class="form-group" aria-labelledby="downloadHeading">
          <h2 class="panel-title" id="downloadHeading">
            <span class="panel-title-label"><%- include('partials/step', { number: '01' }) %>Download</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="group-content">
            <p class="wii-app-lead">
              A free app for the Homebrew Channel. It works with every controller you can connect to a
              Wii, and with a USB keyboard.
            </p>
            <div class="wii-app-actions">
              <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="<%= downloadUrl %>">Download PictoCard for Wii &darr;</a>
              <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="<%= sourceUrl %>">Source code on GitHub</a>
            </div>
            <p class="field-hint">
              Version <%= version %> &middot; Homebrew Channel package (.zip) &middot;
              <a href="<%= releasesUrl %>">All releases</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <figure class="wii-app-shot">
          <img src="/images/wii-app/compose.png" width="852" height="480"
               alt="PictoCard for Wii showing the card editor with a live preview" />
          <figcaption><strong>The Wii app, not the website.</strong> This is the card editor on a TV, with the same live preview as pictocard.net.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <section class="form-group" aria-labelledby="installHeading">
        <h2 class="panel-title" id="installHeading">
          <span class="panel-title-label"><%- include('partials/step', { number: '02' }) %>Install</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="group-content">
          <ol class="wii-app-steps">
            <li>Extract <code>PictoCard-Wii.zip</code> to the root of your SD card or USB drive. It adds <code>apps/PictoCard</code>.</li>
            <li>Put the SD card or USB drive in your Wii and open the Homebrew Channel.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>PictoCard</strong>. Your Wii needs to be connected to the Internet.</li>
            <li>To receive letters on a Wii Message Board, that Wii adds PictoCard as a friend once. You can do that from the app or on the <a href="/wii">Add PictoCard to your Wii</a> page.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="form-group" aria-labelledby="featuresHeading">
        <h2 class="panel-title" id="featuresHeading">
          <span class="panel-title-label"><%- include('partials/step', { number: '03' }) %>What it can do</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="group-content wii-app-features">
          <div>
            <h3>Cards and letters</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Email a PictoCard, or send a letter to any Wii Message Board.</li>
              <li>Use any photo on your SD card or USB drive: JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF or BMP.</li>
              <li>Add a Mii from your Wii's Mii Channel, with an expression.</li>
              <li>Every font, text color, background and Wii letterhead from the website.</li>
              <li>Live preview and a final review before anything is sent.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Controllers</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Wii Remote, with the pointer, Nunchuk or Classic Controller</li>
              <li>GameCube controller</li>
              <li>Wii U GamePad and Wii U Pro Controller (on Wii U)</li>
              <li>DualShock 3 over USB</li>
              <li>USB keyboard for typing, or the on-screen keyboard</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <figure class="wii-app-shot wii-app-shot-wide">
        <img src="/images/wii-app/review.png" width="852" height="480"
             alt="PictoCard for Wii showing a Wii Message Board letter before it is sent" />
        <figcaption><strong>The Wii app, not the website.</strong> Review a Wii Message Board letter before sending it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  </body>
</html>
